# playAble

Live-performance UI for Ableton Live. Each **scene = song**. Node/Koa server bridges browser ↔ Ableton via **AbletonOSC (UDP/OSC)** — not MIDI or Live API.

**Full context:** read `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` before exploring the codebase.

## Core features

1. **Songs** — start/stop scenes; auto-stop on playback end, slots ended, or timer
2. **Mixer** — per-track mute/volume; settings persist per **song title** (not index) + global defaults in `data/song-profiles.json`; only saved while that song is actively playing
3. **PDF lyrics** — `data/song-docs/{title}.pdf`; auto-opens in iframe modal on scene start; fuzzy title matching in `client/app.js`

## Key paths

- `src/domain/liveService.js` — scene start/stop, mix apply/save, OSC
- `src/domain/songProfileStore.js` — `song-profiles.json`
- `src/api/routes.js` — REST API
- `client/app.js` — UI (songs, mixer, library, doc modal)

## Coding style

- **Favor ES6/ESNext** over legacy vanilla JavaScript in both `client/` and `src/`
- Use ES modules (`import`/`export`), `const`/`let`, `async`/`await`, arrow functions, destructuring, template literals, optional chaining, etc.
- Avoid `var`, IIFEs, and callback pyramids when modern syntax is clearer
- Client loads as `<script type="module">` — no bundler; keep browser-native ESM

## Run

`npm run dev` → http://127.0.0.1:3000 (Node 20+, AbletonOSC in Live)
